{
  "description": "Nikulin's 75 even indefinite 2-elementary lattices (Theorem 1.14.2). Each triple (r, a, delta) is realised by the listed direct sum of standard building blocks. All 75 constructions verified in Sage via discriminant_group().invariants() and quadratic_product() integrality check.",
  "source": "V.V. Nikulin (1979); pyramid from Alexeev et al. (2022) arXiv:2208.10383 Fig. 1.",
  "delta_definition": "delta = 0 iff q([v]) in Z for all [v] in A_L (the discriminant group); equivalently, the discriminant quadratic form takes only integral values.",
  "additivity_theorems": {
    "r": "r(L \u2295 M) = r(L) + r(M)",
    "a": "a(L \u2295 M) = a(L) + a(M)  [when both factors are 2-elementary]",
    "delta": "delta(L \u2295 M) = max(delta(L), delta(M))"
  },
